title: Single-file builds
intro: Build Game makes one exe that carries everything, or a small one for players with .NET.
project: Platformer | Jump Kit

chapter: One file, nothing to install | Game > Build Game
say: Here's the Platformer template, ready to share. Builds used to be a folder of four hundred files. Now they're one.
explain: menu:Game | The Game menu | Both kinds of build live in the Game menu.
build: standalone
say: That's it: one exe of about sixty megabytes, with .NET built in, so players just double click it. The game's scenes, art and compiled scripts ride along inside the file.

chapter: Small builds | Game > Build Small Game
say: If your players already have the .NET Desktop Runtime, there's a smaller option.
build: small
say: Build Small Game makes a four megabyte exe instead. Both sit side by side in the project's Build folder, so you can ship either.
say: The first time a build runs, it unpacks its content once to a cache, and plays from there.
